    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "A subgroup H of a free group F is called inert if r(H ∩ K) ⩽ r(K) for\nevery K ⩽ F ; and compressed if r(H) ⩽ r(K) for every H ⩽ K ⩽ F .\n   Is it true that compressed subgroups are inert?                              E. Ventura\n  ∗ Yes, it is true (A. Jaikin-Zapirain, Preprint, 2024, https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.\n09515).",
